Emacsvox News -- History Of User-Visible Changes

Maintained by Emacsvox Contributors.

* Emacsvox Unreleased --- Current User-Visible Changes

Released notes are preserved in [[file:NEWS-2026.9.2][NEWS for Emacsvox 2026.9.2]].

** Aural Home retains context and unfinished work

~C-e H~ remembers the source item as well as its buffer.  Moving the source
cursor does not retarget explanation or remapping; ~C-c C-o~ in Home returns
to the captured item.  Reopen ~C-e H~ from an ordinary buffer to adopt a new
target.  Help and Home retain their return context and selected row.

Buffer rule editors preserve separate drafts for each source buffer, and
reopening an editor or the same tuned voice preserves unfinished changes.
Generated current-item remaps recheck their source before applying.  Current
explanation and remapping no longer use unrelated earlier feedback; retained
historical presentations remain available through Recent Feedback.

** Consistent Aural navigation and actions

Settings lists speak the name and state together when moving vertically.
Child managers retain their row and column on reopening; Help returns to
its exact origin.  ~C-c C-a~ offers named actions and ~S~ stops previews.
The rule editor now uses ~n/p~ for movement, ~N~ for Add and ~P~ for Preview.
~RET~ opens details or a child list; profiles are applied with ~a~.
Palette ~P~ auditions its voices, while ~RET~ browses them.  Stopping or
interrupting an exact-voice sequence prevents late callbacks restarting it.
